 \section{Discussion and Conclusion}
 Our results make instruction consistency a necessary complement to task performance. Following SIMPLER's controlled-simulation approach~\citep{li2025simpler}, repeating a task from the same physical start reveals failures that favorable wording can conceal. Opposing effects across relations also caution against treating TF as a universal prompting solution.
